{
  "id": "behaviorally-anchored-rating-scale",
  "term": "behaviorally anchored rating scale",
  "definition": "A behaviorally anchored rating scale is an assessment tool that rates performance or engagement by linking score points to specific observable behaviors. In this source, it is used to judge how operating-room staff carry out the WHO Surgical Safety Checklist by observing their behavior during the checklist process.",
